## Server events

| Event | Args | When |
|---|---|---|
| `lw-core:ready` | — | Boot complete, DB live, migrations run |
| `lw-core:playerConnected` | `source, session` | Session created, no character yet |
| `lw-core:characterSelected` | `source, stateId` | Character attached to session |
| `lw-core:characterUnloaded` | `source, prevStateId` | Character detached |
| `lw-core:playerLogout` | `source` | Player returned to character selection |
| `lw-core:playerDropped` | `source, session, reason` | Player disconnected — session still readable during handlers |
| `lw-core:permissionsApplied` | `source, reason` | All contributors done (`'complete'`, `'timeout'`, `'immediate'`) |

## Client events

| Event | Args | When |
|---|---|---|
| `lw-core:sessionReady` | `sessionData` | Server confirmed session is live |
| `lw-core:enterCharacterSelection` | — | Server triggered logout |

---

## Event order on disconnect

1. `lw-core:characterUnloaded` — save character data here
2. `lw-core:playerDropped` — session still readable
3. Session destroyed

## Event order on logout

1. `lw-core:characterUnloaded` — save character data here
2. `lw-core:playerLogout` — logout-specific cleanup
3. Player reassigned to private routing bucket
4. Client receives `lw-core:enterCharacterSelection`

---

## Permission contributor pattern

Resources that contribute character-level ACE permissions must:

1. Call `RegisterPermissions` on start
2. Call `RegisterPermissionContributor` on start
3. Listen to `lw-core:characterSelected`
4. Resolve the character's roles from their own data
5. Call `GrantRoles(source, roles)`
6. Call `DoneContributing(source, GetCurrentResourceName())`

Permissions are applied atomically once all contributors call done or the timeout fires. Never apply ACE directly — always go through this API.

